{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>When you rise</b> — this verse is joined to what comes after it. R. Moses said: the meaning of the verse is thus: when you execute judgment upon the men of wrath, \"all human wrath confesses you.\" And the sense is: every man in his wrath fears you. And in my opinion: when human wrath confesses to you — and these are the enemies besieging Jerusalem — then the remnant of wraths you gird and bind, and they are under your authority, to release from them according to your desire."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 76, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:40.949823920Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}